# Networking

## Return Types

All API calls return `TaskEither<Failure, T>` — never `Future<T>` in repositories.

## Dio Instances

| Instance | Name | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| Authenticated | `'authDio'` | All feature API calls |
| Raw | `'rawDio'` | Token refresh only (avoids interceptor loop) |

Never instantiate `Dio` directly in features — use `sl<ApiClientImpl>()`.

## Interceptor Chain (authDio)

```
AcceptLanguage → Auth → RetryOnTimeout → TimeoutError → Logging
```

## Error Handling

- `ErrorMapper.mapError()` is the single entry point for `DioException → Failure`
- Sealed `Failure` hierarchy — never expose `DioException` beyond `ErrorMapper`
- Presentation resolves i18n keys via `ErrorMessages.*` constants

## Token Refresh

Handled exclusively in `AuthInterceptor` — never manually in features.

## Connectivity

Wrap repo calls in `NetworkGuard.execute()`.

## Timeouts

15s default — only override with a documented reason.

## BLoC Rule

Never call Dio directly from BLoC — always via `ApiClientImpl` through UseCase → Repository.
